  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the most important uncertainty is whether a standard multimodal pipeline (combining RNA and image features) provides a viable and competitive baseline. config_001 uses the most established RNA encoder (scgpt), the strongest pre-trained image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), the simplest profile setting (singleprofile, removing aggregation as a confound), and a simple weighted fusion. This makes it a clean, 'default' multimodal reference point. It is the best first experiment because: (1) it tests the core hypothesis of the study—that multimodal fusion is beneficial—using well-validated components so that any result is not confounded by an unusual encoder choice; (2) it establishes a performance anchor against which all subsequent multimodal variants (multiprofile, different fusion, different encoders) and single-modality baselines (image-only config_017, RNA-only config_011) can be directly compared; and (3) by keeping the design simple (singleprofile, weighted fusion), it isolates the fundamental question of whether the two modalities are complementary before adding complexity. This maximizes the information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

